---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocMock from '../../../components/DocMock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'on-device',          text: 'On-device data' },
  { id: 'cloud-data',         text: 'Cloud data (opt-in)' },
  { id: 'what-we-never-do',  text: 'What we never do' },
  { id: 'controls',           text: 'Your in-app controls' },
  { id: 'third-party',        text: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'your-rights',        text: 'Your rights' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Privacy and Data Model"
  description="A plain-English explanation of what data BudgetBaby stores, where it goes, what we never do, and which third-party services are used."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/docs/privacy-and-data-model"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Privacy and Data Model</h1>
    <p class="docs-summary">
      BudgetBaby is local-first: your budget data lives on your device by default and never
      leaves without your explicit action. This page explains exactly what data exists,
      where it goes, and what third-party services are involved.
    </p>

    <h2 id="on-device">On-device data</h2>
    <p>
      All your budget data is stored locally using SwiftData, encrypted at rest by iOS
      using your device passcode. No account or internet connection is required for any
      core budgeting feature.
    </p>
    <p>What is stored on your device:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>All transactions, categories, payment methods, and notes you enter</li>
      <li>Budget periods: dates, income, allocations, and carry-forward settings</li>
      <li>Recurring bills and subscriptions</li>
      <li>Savings goals and goal contributions</li>
      <li>Money pool starting balances</li>
      <li>App settings and preferences</li>
      <li>Reminder configuration</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      None of this data is sent to our servers unless you explicitly enable cloud backup
      or cloud sync in Settings.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Anonymous crash reporting.</strong> BudgetBaby uses Firebase Crashlytics to collect anonymous crash reports. These contain a stack trace (which lines of code failed) and device metadata (model, iOS version). They never contain transaction data, amounts, descriptions, or any personally identifiable information.
      <br /><br />
      You can opt out at any time inside the app: <strong>Settings → Privacy</strong> has a single toggle that turns off both crash reports and any product telemetry. When the toggle is off, RevenueCat (the subscription provider) also runs in anonymous mode — your purchase history is still tracked for restoring purchases, but no user ID is associated with it.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Privacy toggle" caption="A single switch controls analytics, crash reports, and RevenueCat anonymity.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Privacy</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-good">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Local-only mode</strong><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#A7F3D0;">Crash reports, analytics, and product telemetry are off. RevenueCat runs anonymously.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">What's on / off</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Anonymous crash reports</span><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px;">✗</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Product analytics</span><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px;">✗</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Subscription telemetry</span><span style="color:#FBBF24; font-size:14px;">Anon</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Cloud backup</span><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px;">Off</span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="cloud-data">Cloud data (opt-in)</h2>
    <p>Two cloud features exist, both fully opt-in and both requiring a signed-in account:</p>
    <h3>Cloud backup</h3>
    <p>
      When you create a cloud backup, your data is encrypted on your device using AES-256-GCM
      before upload. The encryption key is stored in your iOS Keychain and synced to your
      other devices via iCloud Keychain. We store the encrypted blob on our servers.
      We cannot decrypt or read the contents.
    </p>
    <h3>Cloud sync</h3>
    <p>
      Cloud sync transmits your data over TLS and stores it encrypted at rest in Firebase Firestore.
      Sync is rolling out progressively and is opt-in at Settings → Account → Cloud Sync.
      When enabled, your budget data is stored in Firestore associated with your account ID.
    </p>
    <h3>Account data</h3>
    <p>When you create an account, we store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your authentication identifier (Apple ID, Google ID, or email address)</li>
      <li>A unique account ID used to associate your backups and sync data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not store passwords directly. Authentication is handled by Firebase Auth, which means your credentials go to Firebase, not to our own servers.</p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Cloud features" caption="Both backup and sync are explicit opt-in. Off by default.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Account</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Cloud backup</strong><span class="dm-toggle on purple"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-help">AES-256-GCM before upload. Key in iOS Keychain.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Cloud sync</strong><span class="dm-toggle"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-help">Rolling out. Encrypted at rest in Firestore. <span class="dm-pill purple" style="font-size:6.5px;">Beta</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Account</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Email</span><span class="dm-row-meta">tim@example.com</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Provider</span><span class="dm-row-meta">Sign in with Apple</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Account ID</span><span class="dm-row-meta">acc_a1b2…</span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="what-we-never-do">What we never do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We do not connect to your bank.</strong> BudgetBaby is entirely manual entry. No bank credentials, no Plaid, no open banking APIs.</li>
      <li><strong>We do not sell your data.</strong> Your data is yours. We do not sell, license, or share it with advertisers or data brokers.</li>
      <li><strong>We do not serve ads.</strong> There are no ads in BudgetBaby and no ad network SDKs embedded in the app.</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot read your cloud backups.</strong> Backups are encrypted before upload with a key only your device holds.</li>
      <li><strong>We do not read your transaction data.</strong> Our support team never accesses individual transaction amounts, descriptions, or budget values. Support diagnostics contain only anonymous counts and metadata.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Five guarantees" caption="Promises baked into the architecture, not just policy.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">What we never do</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px; width:14px;">✗</span><span class="dm-row-label" style="font-size:9px;">Connect to your bank</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px; width:14px;">✗</span><span class="dm-row-label" style="font-size:9px;">Sell your data</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px; width:14px;">✗</span><span class="dm-row-label" style="font-size:9px;">Serve ads</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px; width:14px;">✗</span><span class="dm-row-label" style="font-size:9px;">Read your cloud backups</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px; width:14px;">✗</span><span class="dm-row-label" style="font-size:9px;">Read your transactions</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-good" style="margin-top:auto; text-align:center;">
          <span class="dm-icon shield" style="width:24px; height:24px; margin:0 auto;">✓</span>
          <div class="dm-h2" style="margin-top:4px;">Verifiable by design</div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="text-align:center; color:#A7F3D0;">Encryption keys live only on your devices.</div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="controls">Your in-app controls</h2>
    <p>Three places in Settings give you direct control over your data:</p>

    <h3>Settings → Privacy</h3>
    <p>
      A single toggle controls analytics and crash reports. When off, both Firebase
      Crashlytics and any product telemetry stop. RevenueCat (the subscription provider)
      switches to anonymous mode — purchases still work and can still be restored, but
      no user identifier is associated with your subscription.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Activity log" caption="Every save, edit, and delete is timestamped and undoable.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Activity</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,0.12); border-color:rgba(167,139,250,0.4);">
            <span class="dm-icon target">T</span>
            <span class="dm-row-label">Logged $42.18 · Groceries<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Today, 6:14 PM</div></span>
            <span class="dm-pill purple">Undo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon target">T</span><span class="dm-row-label">Edited bill: Rent<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Today, 5:50 PM</div></span><span class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">·</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon target">T</span><span class="dm-row-label">Marked Rent paid<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Mar 1</div></span><span class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">·</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon star">G</span><span class="dm-row-label">Goal contribution +$200<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Feb 28</div></span><span class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">·</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Log lives on-device only. Never uploaded.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h3>Settings → Activity &amp; History</h3>
    <p>
      Activity Log shows every save, edit, and delete in your data, with the latest
      undoable. Tap the most recent entry's <strong>Undo</strong> button to revert it
      (transactions, allocations, transfers, savings deposits, and other reversible
      actions are supported). The log is on-device only — it never leaves your phone.
    </p>

    <h3>Settings → Security</h3>
    <p>
      An optional biometric lock (Face ID or Touch ID) can be required to open the app
      or to perform destructive actions like wiping data. The recovery code wizard
      lets you generate and store a one-time fallback code in case biometrics fail
      after a device change.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Security" caption="Optional Face ID lock and a recovery wizard for biometric edge cases.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Security</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Require Face ID</strong><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-help">On launch and before destructive actions.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Hide amounts when locked</strong><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Recovery code</strong><span class="dm-pill green">Set</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help">Generated Mar 02 · stored only by you</div>
          <div class="dm-btn dm-btn-secondary" style="margin-top:4px;">Regenerate</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon danger">!</span><span class="dm-row-label">Wipe data after 10 fails</span><span class="dm-toggle"></span></div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="third-party">Third-party services</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Data received</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Firebase Auth</strong> (Google)</td>
            <td>Account authentication (sign in, sign out, account deletion)</td>
            <td>Your email or Apple/Google identity token. No budget data.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> (Google)</td>
            <td>Anonymous crash reporting to help us fix bugs</td>
            <td>Crash stack traces, device model, iOS version. No personal or financial data.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Firebase Analytics</strong> (Google)</td>
            <td>Anonymous usage events (which screens are used, not what is in them)</td>
            <td>Screen names, feature interaction events. No transaction or budget data.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Firebase Firestore</strong> (Google)</td>
            <td>Cloud sync storage (opt-in only)</td>
            <td>Your encrypted budget data, associated with your account ID.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>RevenueCat</strong></td>
            <td>Subscription management and Premium entitlement verification</td>
            <td>App Store receipt, subscription status, and a RevenueCat user ID. No financial data.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Apple StoreKit</strong></td>
            <td>In-app purchase processing</td>
            <td>Handled entirely by Apple. We never see your payment information.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Firebase and RevenueCat have their own privacy policies. Links to those policies are in our
      <a href="/budgetbaby/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Third parties" caption="Each service receives only what's needed for its job.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span></span><span class="dm-bar-title">Third-party services</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon shield">F</span><span class="dm-row-label">Firebase Auth<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Sign-in only</div></span><span class="dm-pill green">No tx</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon shield">F</span><span class="dm-row-label">Crashlytics<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Anonymous crashes</div></span><span class="dm-pill green">No PII</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon shield">F</span><span class="dm-row-label">Firestore<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Cloud sync (opt-in)</div></span><span class="dm-pill purple">Encrypted</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon shield">R</span><span class="dm-row-label">RevenueCat<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Subscriptions</div></span><span class="dm-pill green">No $</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon shield">A</span><span class="dm-row-label">StoreKit<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Apple</div></span><span class="dm-pill green">Apple-only</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Full disclosures live in the Privacy Policy.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access.</strong> All your budget data is visible and searchable directly in the app.</li>
      <li><strong>Export.</strong> Use Settings → Export Data to download your data as a CSV at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete local data.</strong> Settings → About → Reset All Data permanently removes all on-device data.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete cloud data.</strong> Settings → Account → Manage Backups → Delete All Backups removes all cloud backups.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete your account.</strong> Settings → Account → Delete Account removes your authentication record and all associated cloud data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For complete step-by-step deletion instructions, see the <a href="/budgetbaby/delete-data">Delete Your Data</a> page.
      For the full legal text, see the <a href="/budgetbaby/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      For a deeper look at security and architecture, see the <a href="/budgetbaby/trust">Trust page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
